1
00:00:00,817 --> 00:00:07,717
USGLoc: uncertainty-aware semantic visual localization from
3D Gaussian splatting.

2
00:00:09,317 --> 00:00:13,592
A robot fuses every camera pose into its state estimator.

3
00:00:13,942 --> 00:00:18,317
That fusion is only as good as the uncertainty attached to
each pose.

4
00:00:18,667 --> 00:00:23,317
Yet most localizers return a single pose, with no
confidence.

5
00:00:23,667 --> 00:00:26,292
How much should the robot trust this pose?

6
00:00:28,700 --> 00:00:33,225
USGLoc keeps one uncertainty channel, from the map to the
pose.

7
00:00:33,575 --> 00:00:40,000
Every Gaussian carries a Dempster-Shafer belief, with an
explicit vacuity mass for missing evidence.

8
00:00:40,350 --> 00:00:46,975
The query passes through the same head, and vacuity gates
semantic matching into a few pose hypotheses.

9
00:00:47,325 --> 00:00:52,050
A render-and-match correction then snaps each hypothesis
into place.

10
00:00:52,400 --> 00:00:57,525
Rendered like color, vacuity also weights the refinement,
pixel by pixel.

11
00:00:57,875 --> 00:01:06,050
A tempered Laplace approximation turns each hypothesis into
a covariance: a Gaussian mixture over SE(3).

12
00:01:08,650 --> 00:01:12,725
Demo one: the Stairs scene of 7Scenes, our best case.

13
00:01:13,075 --> 00:01:16,350
Left: the query and the map rendered at our pose.

14
00:01:16,700 --> 00:01:21,425
Right: our pose and its two-sigma covariance, with ACE and
Marepo.

15
00:01:21,775 --> 00:01:29,500
Here our median error is 1.4 centimeters, against 2.9 for
ACE and 3.4 for GSplatLoc.

16
00:01:29,850 --> 00:01:35,050
On the queries where we fail, our reported uncertainty is 15
times larger.

17
00:01:37,650 --> 00:01:42,300
Demo two: Apartment 2 Kitchen of 12Scenes, our best case
there.

18
00:01:42,650 --> 00:01:50,825
Our median error is 0.4 centimeters, against 0.6 for ACE and
0.7 for GSplatLoc.

19
00:01:51,175 --> 00:01:57,575
Across the 12 scenes, USGLoc is more accurate than every
baseline shown on 7 of them.

20
00:01:59,792 --> 00:02:02,792
Demo three: what the uncertainty is worth.

21
00:02:03,142 --> 00:02:07,367
We keep only the half of the queries that each method trusts
most.

22
00:02:07,717 --> 00:02:20,867
Our median error drops from 0.77 to 0.50 centimeters; ACE
drops to 0.60 with a PnP covariance, and to 0.70 with its
inlier count.

23
00:02:21,217 --> 00:02:25,192
The poses USGLoc trusts most are the most accurate.

24
00:02:26,817 --> 00:02:35,192
On 7Scenes, USGLoc has the lowest average error and the
highest success rate at two centimeters and two degrees.

25
00:02:35,542 --> 00:02:40,117
And it is the only method here that reports how much to
trust its pose.

26
00:02:41,733 --> 00:02:45,508
USGLoc: a pose, and how much to trust it.

27
00:02:45,858 --> 00:02:48,633
Code and video are linked in the paper.
